.\"VERSION : $Revision$"
.\"DATE    : $Date$"
.\"FILE    : pam.1"
.TH pam 1
.SH NAME
.B pam
- Dirac job control script
.SH SYNOPSIS
pam [-copy "file1 file2 ..."] [-get "file1 file2"] [-debug] 
[-incmo] [-utcmo] [-infck] [-utfck] [-mw "mem"] [-nw "mem"] 
[-rmscr] [-rmwrk] [-run "name"] [-scr "name"] [-mpi "n"] 
[-nice] [-notify] [-user "user"] [-dirac "cmd"]
mol[.mol] menu[.inp]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pam
is the job control script to Dirac. It copies files to working directory,
starts 
.B
dirac,
and moved files back, etc.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP 5
.B -copy file
Copy file 'file' to work area
If
.B
-copy
is specified more than once, all files specified will be copied.
.TP 5
.B -get file
Get file 'file' from work area.
.B
-get
is incremental, just as 
.B
-copy
.TP 5
.B -debug
Run 
.B dirac
in debugger
.TP 5
.B -incmo
Copy file 'DFCOEF' (DHF molecular orbital coefficients) to work area. This is an alias for
.B -copy DFCOEF
.TP 5
.B -utcmo
Get file 'DFCOEF' (DHF molecular orbital coefficients) from work area. This is an alias for
.B -get DFCOEF
.TP 5
.B -infck
Copy file 'DFFCK2' to work area, for restart on 2-electron Fock matrix. This is an alias for
.B -copy DFFCK2
.TP 5
.B -utfck
Get file 'DFFCK2' from work area. This is an alias for
.B -get DFFCK2
.TP 5
.B
-mw "mem"
Set working memory (in megawords) for master. The size of the working memory
can also be specified through the environment variable
.B DIRWRK. 
If this is not set, the default memory size specified in 
.B configure
is used.
.TP 5
.B
-nw "mem"
Set working memory (in megawords) for nodes. The size of the working memory
can also be specified through the environment variable
.B DIRNOD. 
If neither 
.B -nw
nor 
.B DIRNOD
are set, then the memory size from
.B -mw
or
.B DIRWRK
is used. If none of these are set, the default memory size is used.
.TP 5
.B -rmscr
Delete directory with work area before starting job.
.TP 5
.B -rmwrk
Delete directory with work area when job is finished.
.TP 5
.B -run "name"
File suffix for output file. The default is "
.B .out".
.TP 5
.B -scr "name"
Set scratch directory. Default scratch directory is prompted when configuring
.B Dirac.
.TP 5
.B -mpi "n"
Execute parallel version of 
.B Dirac
with n nodes. 
.TP 5
.B -nice
Execute the job with 'nice' or 'npri' (on SGI).
.TP 5
.B -notify
Send user a mail upon completion of the job.
.TP 5
.B -user "user"
Send the above e-mail to "user".
.TP 5
.B -dirac "cmd"
Use alternate 
.B Dirac executable
"cmd" instead of the default 
.B dirac.x.
.TP 5
.B -help
This page.
.TP 5
.B mol[.mol]
The molecule file (must be given).
.TP 5
.B menu[.inp]
The menu (job) file (must be given).
Refer to the manual 
.B http://dirac.chem.ou.dk/Dirac
for the description of the files.
.PP
.SH FILES
pam
.SH BUGS
None (of course)
